ship-course/articleshow/132614609.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-25T02:09:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132614621,imgsize-82378.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote of the day by Michael Faraday: 'There's nothing quite as frightening as someone who knows...']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132614203.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The danger of absolute certainty lies in its ability to stifle necessary discussions and overlook crucial warning signs. Renowned scientist Michael Faraday emphasized the importance of maintaining doubt and curiosity in our thoughts. Psychological studies reveal that a limited understanding can cause individuals to mistakenly inflate their competence. In leadership, rigid mindsets can have disastrous consequences throughout history. Embracing new information and perspectives is essential for our survival.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/quote-of-the-day-by-michael-faraday-theres-nothing-quite-as-frightening-as-someone-who-knows-they-are-right-and-how-blind-certainty-is-human-natures-most-dangerous-trap/articleshow/132614203.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/quote-of-the-day-by-michael-faraday-theres-nothing-quite-as-frightening-as-someone-who-knows-they-are-right-and-how-blind-certainty-is-human-natures-most-dangerous-trap/articleshow/132614203.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-25T01:54:49+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132614549,imgsize-461724.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote of the day on discretion and self-preservation: 'It's good to know the truth and speak it. Bu